                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(R)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda(R)
            are quasi-inverse functions of each other.
          %p
            By the rules for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+types"} dependent sum types
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product+types"} dependent product types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible"} contractible
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+inverse+functions"} coherent inverse functions
            of each other.
          %h3#indexed_heterogeneous_identity_types Indexed heterogeneous identity types
          %p
            Given the definition of the equivalence type as the type of encodings for one-to-one correspondences, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+heterogeneous+identity+type"} indexed heterogeneous identity type
            is defined by the rule
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi a
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi b
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %msubsup
                        %mo =
                        %mi B
                        %mi p
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≡
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %msubsup
                        %mo =
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} tr
                            %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma \vdash a:A \quad \Gamma \vdash b:A \quad \Gamma \vdash p:a =_A b \quad \Gamma, x:A \vdash B \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma \vdash (x =_B^p y) \equiv (x =_{B(a), B(b)}^{\mathrm{tr}_B(p)} y) \; \mathrm{type}}
          %h3#identity_equivalences_inverse_equivalences_and_composition_of_equivalences Identity equivalences, inverse equivalences, and composition of equivalences
          %p
            The identity equivalence on a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is defined as an equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{id}_A:A \simeq A
            such that for all elements
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                    %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda(\mathrm{id}_A, a) \coloneqq a
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                    %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(\mathrm{id}_A, a) \coloneqq a
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %msubsup
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                        %mi A
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a =_{A, A}^{\mathrm{id}_A} b) \coloneqq (a =_A b)
          %p
            Given an equivalence
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R:A \simeq B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is an equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^{-1}:B \simeq A
            such that for all elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:B
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(R^{-1}, a) \coloneqq \lambda(R, a)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda(R^{-1}, b) \coloneqq \rho(R, b)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %msubsup
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi R
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                  %mi a
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi a
                  %msubsup
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                    %mi R
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b =_{B, A}^{R^{-1}} a \coloneqq a =_{A, B}^R b
          %p
            Given equivalences
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R:A \simeq B
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S:B \simeq C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is an equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \circ R:A \simeq C
            such that for all elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c:C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda(S \circ R, a) \coloneqq \lambda(R, \lambda(S, a))
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(S \circ R, c) \coloneqq \rho(S, \rho(R, c))
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %msubsup
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi R
                  %mi c
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %msubsup
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                    %mi R
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %msubsup
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                    %mi R
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a =_{A, C}^{S \circ R} c \coloneqq \sum_{b:B} (a =_{A, B}^R b) \times (b =_{B, C}^R c)
          %h3#relation_to_universes_and_univalence Relation to universes and univalence
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Russell+universe"} Russell universe
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:U
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B:U
            are equal: by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi U
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A =_U B
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \simeq B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalence axiom
            says that these two types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi U
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A =_U B
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \simeq B
            are the same, which is represented by an equivalence between the two types
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ua
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi U
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{ua}(A, B):(A =_U B) \simeq (A \simeq B)
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tarski+universes"} Tarski universes
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U, \mathrm{El})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi U
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A =_U B
            is the same as
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{El}(A) \simeq \mathrm{El}(B)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ua
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi U
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{ua}(A, B):(A =_U B) \simeq (\mathrm{El}(A) \simeq \mathrm{El}(B))
          %h3#action_on_equivalences Action on equivalences
          %p
            We introduce a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+operator"} modal operator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            to the type theory, which we assume in general not to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent"} idempotent
            or
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic"} monadic
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma \vdash L(A) \; \mathrm{type}}
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            preserves equivalences: given types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ae
                      %mi L
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi L
